-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC # Creating and Managing a Dashboard
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC [Databricks AI/BI](https://www.databricks.com/product/ai-bi) is a new self-service BI tool that expands traditional BI target persona, workflows, and use cases to serve the needs of non-technical business users. The goal is to enable anyone to use data to inform business decisions. The target users do not need to know SQL, how to write code, or how to set up or administer cloud compute or storage. 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC A few things that differentiate AI/BI dashboards from traditional DBSQL dashboards are:
-- MAGIC * **Data model:** queries are not distinct objects in an AI/BI dashboard. In AI/BI, all the content is bundled within the dashboard itself. So, sharing an AI/BI dashboard is as simple as sharing the dashboard itself.
-- MAGIC * **SQL-optional user experience:** AI/BI gives the ability to search for and select a table of interest to automatically create a dataset based on that table. Additional aggregations can be created without SQL. However, SQL remains a first-class option for those who prefer.
-- MAGIC * **Publish and share:** the initial design stage of a dashboard starts in  draft mode. When ready for distribution, it can be published. Changes to the draft dashboard do not impact the published version. Published dashboards can be shared with anyone in the organization, including those outside the Databricks workspace. 
-- MAGIC * **Visualization library and configuration:** AI/BI dashboards constrain the new visualization library and configuration experience.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## Prerequisites
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC In this notebook, we will build AI/BI dashboards based on the TPC-DI dataset. In order to follow along, you must have run through the TPC-DI ingestion process, as outlined in the *02.1 Ingesting Data* notebook.

